# Outfit window Shader row (client/MANIFEST.md "Outfit shaders in the Outfit window", BASE.md 26). The 10.98 outfit window packet already lists the shaders the character owns (the server sends them, protocolgameparse reads them with GameOutfitShaders, game_outfit got them as shaderList) but this window never showed them: it had no Shader row, so no shader could be picked. Lua and OTUI only (no C++): data/styles/40-outfitwindow.otui gets a Shader row in the Familiar row's place (10.98 has no familiars; the window shows one of the two); modules/game_outfit/outfit.lua lists "None" and the owned shaders (each button previews the current outfit with that shader; the search box filters them), keeps the pick in the preview and the set-outfit packet, keeps it across presets (presets store no shader) and sends only a shader of the list (else ""), since the server refuses the whole outfit change for a shader the character does not own. The logic is OutfitShaderList of the overlay module game_chaosshaders (outfitshaderlist.lua, tested by outfitshaderlist_test.lua); without that module the row stays hidden. updateAppearanceText also ignores a key with no row (a worn wings id). Applies after 0001-0044.
